{"file":"design-skills-1.0.0-v1.zip","bytes":527664,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"design-skills","description":"Ten UX and design skills that give coding agents deep knowledge of established design frameworks: research, critique, accessibility, journey mapping, design systems, strategy, interaction design, design ops, UX writing, and visual elevation.","version":"1.0.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/cuellarfr/design-skills","homepage":"https://cuellarfr.github.io/design-skills/","keywords":["design","ux","accessibility","design-systems","ux-research","ux-writing","interaction-design"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/accessibility-audit/SKILL.md","name":"accessibility-audit","description":"Conduct accessibility audits against WCAG 2.2 guidelines. Evaluate pages, components, and flows for conformance at A, AA, and AAA levels. Identify issues, assess severity, provide code fixes, and generate audit reports. Covers automated testing, manual testing, keyboard navigation, screen reader compatibility, color contrast, and semantic HTML.","headings":["Accessibility Audit","Core Principle","WCAG Conformance Levels","What's New in WCAG 2.2 (vs 2.1)","How to Run an Accessibility Audit","The 5-Layer Audit Process","Severity Scoring","Impact Scale","WCAG Level as Priority Signal","Triage Framework","The 80/20: Most Common Issues","Semantic HTML: The Foundation","Quick Audit Checklist (For Code Reviews)","HTML Structure","Images","Forms","Interactive Elements","Color and Contrast"],"name_hint":"accessibility · 审查","description_zh":"按WCAG 2.2的A、AA与AAA级审查页面、组件和流程，评估问题严重度并提供代码修复与报告，涵盖自动及手工测试、键盘、读屏、对比度和语义HTML。"},{"path":"skills/design-critique/SKILL.md","name":"design-critique","description":"Evaluate UI designs against usability heuristics, UX laws, interaction patterns, interaction design principles, information architecture, and content quality. Conduct heuristic evaluations, structured design critiques, pattern-based reviews, posture analysis, excise audits, IA evaluations, and UX writing reviews. Provides specific, actionable feedback grounded in established principles rather than subjective opinion.","headings":["Design Critique & Evaluation","Core Principle","The Critique Framework","Step 1: Understand Context Before Judging","Step 2: First Impression Scan (5 seconds)","Step 3: Heuristic Pass","Step 4: UX Law Check","Step 5: Interaction Design Review","Step 6: Pattern Review","Step 7: Information Architecture Review","Step 8: Content & Writing Review","Step 9: Synthesize and Prioritize","Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics","Severity Scale for Heuristic Violations","UX Laws Quick Reference","Layout and Visual Design","Decision Making and Choices","Interaction and Input"],"name_hint":"设计 · critique","description_zh":"依据可用性启发式、UX规律、交互原则、信息架构和内容质量开展结构化设计评审，提供有既有原则支撑的具体改进。"},{"path":"skills/design-elevation/SKILL.md","name":"design-elevation","description":"Comprehensive design elevation system that automatically transforms functional visual outputs into polished, professional designs. Use when creating ANY visual output including presentations (pptx), spreadsheets (xlsx), dashboards, reports, HTML artifacts, PDFs, web pages, or data visualizations. Applies systematic design thinking grounded in Tailwind CSS as the canonical design token system. Structures decisions through functional patterns (what users interact with) and perceptual patterns (how the design feels), following Alla Kholmatova's design systems framework. Triggers on ALL requests for visual content creation, ensuring outputs look hand-crafted rather than template-based.","headings":["Design Elevation System","Design Philosophy","Canonical Design Tokens: Tailwind CSS","Activation Protocol","Functional Patterns by Output Type","For Presentations (PPTX)","For Dashboards & Data Visualization","For Documents & Reports","For Web/HTML Artifacts","Perceptual Patterns","Typography Excellence","Color Sophistication","Spatial Systems","Visual Refinement","Design Exemplars","Trimble Modus Override","IBM Carbon Override","Shopify Polaris Override"],"name_hint":"设计 · elevation","description_zh":"系统改进演示、表格、仪表板、报告、HTML、PDF与网页等视觉输出，以Tailwind令牌为规范参考，按功能与感知模式组织设计决定，提升专业视觉质量。"},{"path":"skills/design-ops/SKILL.md","name":"design-ops","description":"Run design sprints, manage handoff, establish team rituals, documentation standards, and design QA processes. Covers the operational side of design — how teams organize work, collaborate with engineering, and ship quality.","headings":["Design Ops & Handoff","Design Sprints","When to Sprint","The 5-Day Structure","Sprint Team","Sprint Rules","Design-to-Development Handoff","Handoff Maturity Levels","What a Complete Handoff Includes","Handoff Anti-Patterns","Team Rituals and Cadences","Core Design Rituals","Running Effective Design Critiques","Handoff Session Structure","Documentation Standards","File Organization","Naming Conventions","Version Control Rules"],"name_hint":"设计 · ops","description_zh":"组织设计冲刺、交接、团队节奏、文档与设计QA，改善设计工程协作和交付。"},{"path":"skills/design-systems/SKILL.md","name":"design-systems","description":"Build, document, and maintain design systems with design tokens, component specifications, pattern libraries, naming conventions, and governance processes. Conduct system audits, define component hierarchies, and establish shared design languages.","headings":["Design Systems","Core Concepts","Two Types of Patterns","Component Hierarchy (Atomic Design)","Design Tokens","When to Build a Design System","Signals You Need One","Signals You Don't (Yet)","The Interface Inventory (5-Step Audit)","Component Specification","Required Fields","The \"Same or Different?\" Decision","Naming Patterns","Principles","Naming Test","Governance","Contribution Model","Pattern Lifecycle"],"name_hint":"设计 · systems","description_zh":"建立、记录和维护设计系统令牌、组件、模式库、命名与治理，开展审计、定义层级并形成共享设计语言。"},{"path":"skills/interaction-design/SKILL.md","name":"interaction-design","description":"Design meaningful interactions, microinteractions, animations, state machines, gesture patterns, error prevention, and product behavior. Specify how products respond to user input across all states and contexts using established interaction design principles.","headings":["Interaction Design","The Microinteraction Framework","Triggers","Rules","Feedback","Loops and Modes","Product Posture","Perpetual Intermediates","Orchestration and Flow","Flow State","Harmonious Interaction Principles (Cooper)","Narrative Structure in Product Design","The Narrative Arc Applied to Products","Three Types of Product Stories","Storymapping Process","Applying the Peak-End Rule","When to Use Storymapping","Excise"],"name_hint":"interaction · 设计","description_zh":"设计交互、微交互、动画、状态机、手势与错误预防，规定产品在不同状态与情境对输入的响应。"},{"path":"skills/journey-mapping/SKILL.md","name":"journey-mapping","description":"Create customer journey maps, service blueprints, experience maps, empathy maps, and other alignment diagrams. Guides diagram type selection, content structure, illustration syntax, and alignment workshops.","headings":["Journey Mapping & Service Design","Core Principle","Diagram Types: When to Use What","Quick Selection Guide","The Mapping Process","Phase 1: Initiate","Phase 2: Investigate","Phase 3: Illustrate","Phase 4: Align","Customer Journey Map: Core Structure","Required Elements","Optional Elements","Service Blueprint: Core Structure","Five Swimlanes","Three Critical Lines","When to Use a Blueprint vs. a Journey Map","Empathy Map: Core Structure","Four Quadrants + Center"],"name_hint":"journey · mapping","description_zh":"创建客户旅程、服务蓝图、体验和共情地图，指导图型、内容、绘制语法与对齐工作坊。"},{"path":"skills/ux-research/SKILL.md","name":"ux-research","description":"Plan, conduct, and analyze UX research using proven methodologies. Use when planning user research, writing interview scripts, creating test plans, recruiting participants, analyzing qualitative data, or synthesizing findings into actionable insights. Covers generative, evaluative, and continuous discovery research with specific frameworks, scoring rubrics, and templates.","headings":["UX Research","When to Use This Skill","Core Principle","Research Types","Generative / Exploratory","Descriptive","Evaluative","Causal","The Research Process","1. Define the Problem","2. Select the Approach","3. Plan and Prepare","4. Recruit Participants","5. Collect Data","6. Analyze Data","7. Report Results","Continuous Discovery","Common Mistakes to Avoid"],"name_hint":"ux · 研究","description_zh":"规划、执行与分析UX研究，编写访谈和测试计划、招募参与者、分析定性资料并形成洞察，覆盖生成、评估与持续探索研究。"},{"path":"skills/ux-strategy/SKILL.md","name":"ux-strategy","description":"Connect design decisions to business outcomes through competitive analysis, opportunity mapping, Jobs to Be Done, outcome-driven discovery, value proposition design, and UX metrics. Shape product direction with strategic frameworks grounded in evidence.","headings":["UX Strategy","Core Framework","Outcomes Over Outputs","Types of Outcomes","Setting Outcomes","Anti-patterns","Opportunity Mapping","The Opportunity Solution Tree (OST)","Writing Good Opportunity Statements","Structuring the Tree","Prioritizing Opportunities","Jobs to Be Done (JTBD)","Core Concept","Job Structure","Job Map (8 Stages)","Finding Underserved Needs","Four Forces of Switching","Competitive Analysis"],"name_hint":"ux · strategy","description_zh":"通过竞品、机会映射、待完成任务、成果导向探索、价值主张和UX指标将设计决策连接业务结果，依据证据塑造方向。"},{"path":"skills/ux-writing/SKILL.md","name":"ux-writing","description":"Create user-centered, accessible interface copy (microcopy) for digital products including buttons, labels, error messages, notifications, forms, onboarding, empty states, success messages, and help text. Use when writing or editing any text that appears in apps, websites, or software interfaces, designing conversational flows, establishing voice and tone guidelines, auditing product content for consistency and usability, reviewing UI strings, or improving existing interface copy. Applies UX writing best practices based on four quality standards — purposeful, concise, conversational, and clear. Includes accessibility guidelines, research-backed benchmarks (sentence length, comprehension rates, reading levels), expanded error patterns, tone adaptation frameworks, and comprehensive reference materials.","headings":["UX Writing","When to Use This Skill","Core UX Writing Principles","The Four Quality Standards","Key Best Practices","UX Text Patterns","Titles","Buttons and Links","Error Messages","Success Messages","Empty States","Form Fields","Notifications","Formatting & Style Conventions","Capitalization","Numbers and Dates","Tense","Abbreviations"],"name_hint":"ux · writing","description_zh":"为按钮、标签、错误、通知、表单、引导和空状态等编写可访问界面文案，按目的、简洁、对话与清晰标准调整语气，并审查产品内容一致性。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Design Skills for AI Agents","Skills","UX Research","Design Critique & Evaluation","Accessibility Audit","Journey Mapping","Design Systems","UX Strategy","Interaction Design","Design Ops & Handoff","UX Writing","Design Elevation","Installation","Any agent — `npx skills`","List available skills before installing","Install a specific skill","Install globally (available across all projects)","Install to a specific agent","Claude Code — as a plugin","Skill Architecture","License"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".gitignore","CLAUDE.md","LICENSE","README.md","index.html","skills/accessibility-audit/SKILL.md","skills/accessibility-audit/examples/audit-walkthrough.md","skills/accessibility-audit/examples/quick-wins.md","skills/accessibility-audit/references/common-issues-and-fixes.md","skills/accessibility-audit/references/testing-tools-and-techniques.md","skills/accessibility-audit/references/wcag-checklist.md","skills/accessibility-audit/templates/accessibility-rules-file.md","skills/accessibility-audit/templates/audit-report-template.md","skills/accessibility